WEBVTT

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.420
Note: IMO we should use the English translation for all the ninja attacks.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.580
It's as though nothing has happened in the Village of Mist.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:38.070
That's right.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:44.580
I'm rather happy to be able to bathe and live with you.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.450
That's sort of frightening in itself.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:55.590
It makes me think that we've really become master and servant.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.600
So you really think like that.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.060
Huh?

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.110
Smoke.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.220
It looks like there's a hot spring over there too.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:09.460
Nope.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.080
That's not a hot spring.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:26.820
This is...

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.250
You're mistaken, Wabisuke.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.330
They're not enemies.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:38.700
Hayato!

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.790
Okashira-san!

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.080
Wabisuke-kun!

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.480
They were attacked in the dark.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.080
The villagers are also master ninja.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.540
They wouldn't go down easily.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.590
But, the enemy was even better.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.590
Was that enemy possibly...

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.590
"Shining by the light of the inferno, the face we saw was that of a Shinobi High teacher."

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.600
The same thing happened to Tsubaki.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:11.010
Apparently this is happening to villages all over the place.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.940
About those teachers...

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.210
They can't have gotten far yet.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.810
It was a man and a woman!

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.350
Do you want some?

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.820
No, my stomach feels a bit bloated.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:34.770
I'm amazed that Fudenoko-sensei can still eat after something like that.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:38.060
I have to build up energy <i>because of that.</i>

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.160
It's not like I killed anyone.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.540
I just burned down a village, right?

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.680
Orders from the Principal?

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:56.680
Marikouji-sensei and Hinata Himawari are apparently nearby.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:59.390
What's wrong?

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:04.530
Those two...

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.600
Luck is not on our side, apparently.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:21.550
It won't change, no matter how many times you look at it.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:24.470
You're not your usual, composed self, Shikimi-chan.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.680
But, I do understand your feelings.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.880
We can't just leave Himawari alone, huh?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.020
That's not it.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:39.890
I just feel bad about being in the dark.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:56.440
When we left the Village of Mist and settled here,

00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:02.450
I thought that we could finally live in peace.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:04.910
A potato.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.680
Nicely baked by the fire.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.810
It's delicious!

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.760
Do you want some?

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.160
Sabisuke... loved baked potatoes.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.050
Speaking of Sabisuke-kun, where is he?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.670
They took him away, along with the villagers.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.650
No way!

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:31.970
That's... because he's slow.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.690
You're really going to your mother's place?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:47.190
We want to find out the truth about our past.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:50.880
We're heading to the Village of Mist.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.750
We might find a clue about Sabisuke's whereabouts.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.070
Let's go, Wabisuke.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:56.430
Yes, sir!

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.350
I hope Sabisuke-kun is safe.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.500
Yeah.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:03.810
We should leave as well.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:04.440
Yes.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.980
Hayato-dono, do you remember?

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:15.950
You told me about your memories of your mother and maple leaves.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:17.290
Yup.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.900
Things like that existed.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.810
I hope Hayato-dono's memories are real.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:43.030
Himawari...

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:47.950
Who goes there?

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:56.930
F-Fudenoko-sensei!

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.360
Obakyuri-sensei?!

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.690
Any messages from Nanafushi...

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:06.870
None?

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:11.140
It's dangerous to continue staying in touch by letter.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:13.810
Nanafushi!

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:15.410
I'm here.

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:20.820
So Shikimi can look really startled too.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.300
It's just ventriloquism.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.560
Why are you playing jokes on me?

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.080
Don't get mad.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.830
If people see us together, you'll be in danger too.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:33.200
So did you discover the location of the enemy?

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:36.420
I suppose it's no use trying to stop you.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.800
There's something I want to investigate.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.640
Follow me.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:53.160
It's in a place like this...

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.410
You're so full of yourself.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.980
You planned to sneak in there alone to find out about Himawari, right?

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:08.970
Then, we'll go with you.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.470
I'll go too.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.410
Yonezawa-kun, I leave Momota to you.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:22.680
W-Wait!

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:34.960
Yonezawa-kun will always be here to protect me.

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:39.460
Yusura-chan...

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:06.460
This way.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.260
The owl is gone!

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:27.850
What does this mean?

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:32.150
It means that allowing yourself to be swayed by your feelings isn't a good idea.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:41.940
Why are you doing this?

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:44.420
We have orders to erase you.

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:48.240
Burning down the village, capturing the villagers...

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.430
Are those all orders?

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.300
That's right.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:53.710
Even though they're fellow ninja!

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:55.050
Yeah!

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.910
We're fellow teachers, right?!

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.820
Obakyuri-sensei is a really nice person, right?!

00:09:58.820 --> 00:09:59.310
No!

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.310
Despite how I look, I'm still a ninja.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:08.040
The point is, do you even know what you're doing?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.340
It's about that...

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.660
If you use too much toilet paper,

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:15.930
you contribute to deforestation and global warming!

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.660
Hayato-dono, I don't understand what you mean.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:23.330
I mean that when you act, you have to take into account the results of your actions.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:28.350
They experimented on humans like they were animals, even remodeled them!

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:34.400
You're helping truly terrible people, you know?

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.600
Do you get that?

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:38.350
Mind Control Technique, huh?

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:43.050
Disturb the enemy, and use the opportunity to take them down.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.090
You're great, Marikouji-sensei.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.190
No...

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:49.560
It's not a ninja technique, just normal persuasion.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.130
We don't buy that!

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:59.570
These are... all the people we fought against!

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:05.870
Good job.

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.310
You can leave now.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:09.040
But...

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.810
I said it's okay, so fall back!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.820
Just do as you're told!

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:19.790
We're running out of time.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.360
Nanafushi!

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:26.060
Komurasaki!

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:29.440
To deceive our foe, we must deceive our friends first.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:32.070
That's the most basic of basic ninja techniques!

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.090
There's only data we've already seen.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:40.580
In the end, it's all for nothing, huh?

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:44.590
Let's infiltrate their security system.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:45.850
Okay, I'll try.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:52.730
What?

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:54.590
Is there something on my face?

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.960
No. You were just in...

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:05.010
Did they notice us?

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:06.500
Let's retreat for now.

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:07.970
Just a bit more...

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:12.980
Komurasaki, give up!

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:15.780
There's no time.

00:12:15.780 --> 00:12:16.880
Wait!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.540
What's wrong, Azami?

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:21.900
Then we'll just fight all the enemies.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.250
Azami!

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.530
There's... nobody?

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:38.550
Tell me!

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:40.540
Why are you chasing after us like this?

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.680
Because you are the "exceptions."

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:46.700
"Exceptions"?

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.750
What... is this?

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.700
Himawari?

00:12:56.060 --> 00:13:00.140
She must've fallen into that jar and shrunk.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:03.460
Himawari, wake up!

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:09.410
"Exceptions"?

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:12.340
You mean because we're normal people?

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:15.340
Just the opposite.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:22.850
You two are test-tube babies who were cloned from pure genes of exceptional quality.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.090
Who'd believe a story like that?!

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:39.180
You were cloned from Nobunaga, and
Himawari-san from his vassal, Ranmaru.

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:39.180
Note: Oda Nobunaga was a 16th century Japanese warlord, who lived a life of continual military conflict.

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:42.330
Uh, Ranmaru was a man.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:48.240
After a few hundred years, their genes meet again as master and vassal.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.340
What a romantic reunion...

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:54.800
Hey, is this the Mind Control Technique?

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:58.950
Do you think something like that could sidetrack us?

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.670
Then, everything makes sense.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:03.350
What?

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:07.650
Why... are our memories fabricated?

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:09.120
Hey, Himawari!

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:13.220
Why must our lives be targeted like this?

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:14.640
It all makes sense now!

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:17.340
It doesn't make sense at all!

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:21.820
Himawari!

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.170
Don't be confused!

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:25.790
Let's run, Himawari!

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.070
Listen, Himawari...

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:31.390
This is Kyuri's tactic to confuse us.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:35.390
I can't believe that I failed to notice something so simple.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.790
You're not listening.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:42.660
Aren't you supposed to protect me?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:47.930
Paper!

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.490
A rat?

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:54.670
It's huge!

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:01.300
What the hell is this?

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:03.310
It's pitch black! I can't see a thing!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:04.850
Let us out!

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:05.850
It's dark in here!

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.820
Hey, let us out!

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:09.570
Causing us so much trouble...

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.090
That was unexpectedly quick.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:15.150
A turtle?

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:16.590
Fudenoko-sensei, behind you!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.100
Is this a time to be worrying about others?

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:23.100
Where is Sabisuke?

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:24.680
Sabisuke?

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.270
Oh, that pipsqueak ninja friend of yours?

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:28.390
Don't you use the word "pipsqueak"!

00:15:28.390 --> 00:15:30.710
We wouldn't tell you even if we knew.

00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:33.840
Then there's no reason for us to let you live.

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:40.320
"Where there's smoke, there's fire."

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:45.490
Stop!

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:46.760
Let us out!

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:48.290
Damn!

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.730
Like I'm gonna let you digest me!

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:53.080
You... Let me out!

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.750
Hayato-dono!

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:54.750
You... You... You...

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:57.060
When will you stop fooling around?

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:03.240
Burn! Burn! Burn!

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:04.740
What now?

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:09.330
Is this one of Himawari's fake memories that someone fabricated?

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:12.250
But, Himawari is projected here.

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:30.080
Is that Takechi?

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:30.770
It is.

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:34.170
Ninja Technique: Three Point Fissure.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.880
What... was that?

00:16:57.880 --> 00:16:59.300
Is it possible that...

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.590
Himawari is a test-tube baby, like us?

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:07.160
That would explain why the child's memories are fabricated.

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:08.650
You're exactly right.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.210
Takechi.

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.500
Principal Yatsugasura!

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:20.450
About ten years ago, the airplane transporting Himawari-san was blown up.

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:29.600
The pharmaceutical company had hatched a plan to take over the ninja training program.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:37.470
They made it look like the government's control committee had made a mistake.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:40.940
Then, the images we saw were footage of the accident?

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:46.000
Luckily, Takechi-sensei saved Himawari-san,

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:52.850
and we secretly entrusted her to a civilian who was beyond the pharmaceutical company's reach.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:57.960
Marikouji Hayato-san was just another excellent gene.

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:01.440
Hayato was also a test-tube baby?

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:06.460
If I'm not mistaken, Hayato's memories were fabricated too, just like Himawari's.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:11.640
As time went on, the pharmaceutical company obtained control of Shinobi High.

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:14.630
You all know what happened afterwards.

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:19.710
Principal Yatsugashira and I were pretending to be on the company's side,

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:22.790
waiting for a chance to fight back.

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:25.440
That was all to mislead the enemy?

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:28.100
Do you think we'd believe that?

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.590
You tried to kill us many times.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:34.860
What you lack is battlefield experience.

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:39.950
We deliberately sent enemies against you to prepare you for the upcoming battle.

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:43.330
That was our intention.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:45.550
That's so reckless!

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.310
So that's the case...

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:56.910
Oh no!

00:18:56.910 --> 00:18:58.780
It's tranquilizing gas.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:04.870
I feel uneasy.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.420
Something has happened to Yusura-chan.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:11.950
I can't wait any longer.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.330
We'll have to force our way in.

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:17.940
Tsukiyohime-san.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:22.510
If you're irritated and get caught,
you won't be able to save the others.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:25.290
Even so, drinking miso soup will...

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:32.970
There's a letter here, Momojiri.

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:36.550
Tell them about this crisis, and ask them to come back.

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:39.610
In, kyou, tou, sha, kai, jin, zai, zen!

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:49.850
Return safely.

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:54.970
O-Ow.

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:57.150
Be a bit more gentle!

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:58.590
Bear with it.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:00.970
Is this guy really a descendant of Nobunaga?

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:04.910
It's hard to think of Nobunaga as a test-tube baby.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:06.260
Isn't it?

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:08.120
Hey, Himawari.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.050
Ranmaru is an important servant of Nobunaga, y'know.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:16.010
It's a stupid joke that we're clones of such famous people.

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:18.140
You shouldn't be so disturbed.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:22.140
Listen, aren't you the ninja that protects me?

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:23.870
You'll fail as a servant if you behave like that.

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:26.930
It's no use.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:27.870
She's not listening.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:33.430
The fastest way to find out is probably to get into the enemy base and check it out.

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:34.430
Yeah.

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:44.570
It stinks!

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.390
What the heck is this all of a sudden?!

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.060
Momota! What's wrong?

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:00.300
A letter?

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:06.290
What does it say?

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:08.630
N-No, it's nothing.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:14.180
"Shikimi-san and the girls infiltrated the enemy base and got caught!

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:20.010
They did it to find out about Himawari's past.

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:25.930
I'm telling you this because I feel you have a responsibility to save them."

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.130
What the...

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:28.770
This is your fault?

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:32.650
We don't know how much truth there is in Tsukiyohime's words.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:39.450
Everyone is doing this for me,
but I'm just thinking about myself.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:41.960
But that can't be helped.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:45.730
Anyone would be shocked if they were told that they were a test-tube baby.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:48.200
You said, "Being disturbed is stupid."

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.050
I'm sure you said that.

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:53.850
I slowly lost my way and caused trouble for Hayato-dono.

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:56.320
I fail as a servant.

00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:59.260
No, you haven't failed.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:01.530
You said, "You fail as a servant."

00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:02.790
I'm sure you said that.

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:04.900
Whose side are you guys on?

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:05.470
Hers.

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:07.340
Hayato-dono...

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.570
Please forgive me for behavior unbecoming of a servant.

00:22:11.510 --> 00:22:15.200
And also, please forgive me for another thing.

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:16.580
What now?

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:22.480
I, Hinata Himawari, will now go to the Village of Mist and save everyone.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:26.590
Please forgive me for leaving you for a short time.

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:30.840
No way.

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:31.480
I won't forgive you.

00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:35.300
If you're going,

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:36.770
I'm going with you.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.650
Hayato-dono...

00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:43.640
Yes, sir.

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:48.610
If you're infiltrating the enemy base,
the more comrades you take, the better.

00:22:48.610 --> 00:22:50.010
Is that the idea?

00:22:53.130 --> 00:22:55.830
Now, let's head for the Village of Mist!

00:24:10.790 --> 00:24:14.300
In order to search for my memories, everybody entered the enemy base,

00:24:14.590 --> 00:24:19.330
where Principal Yatsugashira and Takechi-sensei told them the truth.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:22.870
But the enemy had set traps there.

00:24:22.870 --> 00:24:23.860
Please wait.

00:24:23.860 --> 00:24:26.110
I'll definitely get you all out of there!

00:24:27.220 --> 00:24:31.730
Okashira-san, are you planning a suicidal attack from the front?

00:24:32.150 --> 00:24:33.060
Next time:

00:24:33.060 --> 00:24:36.190
"Rescue! Friends of shinobi go through thick and thin together."

00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:39.150
Hayato-dono, everyone is all right, aren't they?
